WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.871 --> 00:00:13.351
Many districts want to know how a program fits their state's social and emotional learning standards, or their Portrait of a Graduate. This page shows how Fixer Nation lines up. Here's how to use it.

2
00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:24.882
Before you start, read the note. These matches are Fixer Nation's own mapping. They don't mean your state, your district, or CASEL has endorsed or certified our program.

3
00:00:25.384 --> 00:00:34.884
Choose your state from the list, or select it from the buttons. A state appears once our team has checked its standards against the state's own published documents.

4
00:00:35.387 --> 00:00:46.297
At the top, you'll see what kind of framework the state has, the date our team last checked it, and a link to the state's own page. The state's document is always the source of truth.

5
00:00:46.798 --> 00:00:58.208
Below that, each standard is listed with a short summary, and a note of which CASEL competency it relates to. Fixer Nation lessons and games that connect to it are tucked underneath.

6
00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:14.650
Select Where Fixer Nation connects to open it. Each connection is labelled a direct match, where the lesson teaches the same skill, or a supporting connection, where it reinforces part of the standard. Our team writes a short explanation for every one.

7
00:01:15.152 --> 00:01:28.612
Lessons come in versions for different grade levels. Use the menu to show only the versions for elementary, middle, or high school. You can also tick the box to show only standards with a Fixer Nation connection.

8
00:01:29.113 --> 00:01:35.463
Need something to share with a colleague or your curriculum team? Select Print a one-page summary.

9
00:01:35.965 --> 00:01:46.275
It's a single page, sized for a letter sheet, with the state's framework and our connections on it. Use your browser's print command to print it or save it as a P-D-F.
